# Rova web — dev env.
#
# THE ROOT `.env` SERVES THE SPA TOO, in the dev server only (apps/web/vite.config.ts `envDir`): `cp .env.example .env` at
# the repo root is the whole local setup, and this file is reference only. `vite build` and the unit tests do NOT read the
# root .env, so a local production build cannot pick up VITE_DEV_LOGIN=true. Vite exposes ONLY `VITE_`-prefixed variables to the browser.
#
# `VITE_API_URL` is deliberately ABSENT. The SPA calls relative /v1 paths and must be same-origin with the API,
# because authentication rides a `__Host-` session cookie that cannot be set cross-site. Locally the Vite proxy
# provides that (/v1 -> http://localhost:3000, or API_TARGET); deployed, the Cloudflare Pages Function does. An older
# version of this file set VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000, which sends the browser straight to the API and
# silently breaks the cookie.
#
# VITE_APP_ENV=development
#
# Dev login (non-production only): shows a passwordless seeded-account form so QA can sign in without Entra. Set to
# true ONLY on local and non-prod (QA) environments. The API also hard-blocks dev-login when NODE_ENV=production.
# The root .env.example turns it on for local development.
# VITE_DEV_LOGIN=true
